    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d886">

                <pb facs="1070" n="974" xml:id="pg974"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 668.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that your dispatch No.
                    393, of the 14th ultimo, reporting further conversation of the British
                    ambassador at Madrid with the Spanish minister of foreign affairs in regard to
                    the treaty of 1795 and of the Protocol of the 12th of January, 1877, and its
                    alleged abrogation by Spain, has been received.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
